{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recording-tree-036-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/TreeDiscardPurgeTests.cs","line":616,"method":"PurgeTree_ClearsReservationsForTreeKerbals","category":"T1","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/TreeDiscardPurge.cs:173; delete the CrewReservationManager.RecomputeAfterTombstones() call -> still green because the asserted line is TreeDiscardPurge's own Info at :174-175 in the same branch; deleting that :174 Info line -> red","what_it_asserts":"Purging a tree with one in-tree kerbal-death tombstone emits the [CrewReservations] PurgeTree: recomputed reservations after 1 tombstone(s) log line.","why_weak":"The named recompute call is unwitnessed: the matched line is written by TreeDiscardPurge itself, and no reservation is seeded or asserted, so deleting the RecomputeAfterTombstones() call at :173 leaves the cell green. The recompute's only test-visible output here (the no-KerbalsModule Verbose line from CrewReservationManager.RecomputeFromEffectiveLedger) is not asserted.","proposed_action":"Assert the recompute actually ran under the existing verbose sink (CrewReservations RecomputeFromEffectiveLedger line), or seed a reservation tied to the tree kerbal and assert it is released after the purge.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
